{"id":27410,"section":"officeHoldings","title":"Jason Gibbs — City Council Member, The City of Santa Clarita","status":"live","holdingPerson":["#23091 Jason Gibbs"],"holdingOffice":["#18327 City Council Member"],"holdingBody":["#394 The City of Santa Clarita"],"holdingDistrict":["#25155 Santa Clarita City Council, District 3"],"termStart":"December 2024","termStartEdtf":"2024-12","termEnd":"December 2028","termEndEdtf":"2028-12","seatLabel":"District 3","selectionMethod":"appointed","howEnded":"serving","startEvidence":"certified","footnotes":[{"col1":"1","col2":"The term's end is derived. The City lists him as \"Councilmember Jason Gibbs, District 3\" (City of Santa Clarita, City Council, https://santaclarita.gov/city-council/, read 3 October 2026) and says that \"two district seats were voted upon in November 2024, so the remaining three district seats will be up for election starting in November 2026\" (City of Santa Clarita, District Elections, https://santaclarita.gov/districtelections, read 3 October 2026). His at-large term of 2020 ended in December 2024, so his District 3 seat was one of the two elected that November; four years from December 2024 is December 2028. The District 3 canvass is not yet in the archive.","col3":"editorial-2026","number":"1","note":"The term's end is derived. The City lists him as \"Councilmember Jason Gibbs, District 3\" (City of Santa Clarita, City Council, https://santaclarita.gov/city-council/, read 3 October 2026) and says that \"two district seats were voted upon in November 2024, so the remaining three district seats will be up for election starting in November 2026\" (City of Santa Clarita, District Elections, https://santaclarita.gov/districtelections, read 3 October 2026). His at-large term of 2020 ended in December 2024, so his District 3 seat was one of the two elected that November; four years from December 2024 is December 2028. The District 3 canvass is not yet in the archive.","source":"editorial-2026"},{"col1":"2","col2":"County of Los Angeles Registrar-Recorder/County Clerk, final list of cancelled elections, November 5, 2024, https://content.lavote.gov/docs/rrcc/documents/cancelled-elections-november-2024.pdf: \"Santa Clarita (Council District 3)\" is listed under \"appointment in lieu of election due to insufficiency of candidates.\" He was the only candidate, so no vote was taken and he was appointed to the seat.","col3":"editorial-2026","number":"2","note":"County of Los Angeles Registrar-Recorder/County Clerk, final list of cancelled elections, November 5, 2024, https://content.lavote.gov/docs/rrcc/documents/cancelled-elections-november-2024.pdf: \"Santa Clarita (Council District 3)\" is listed under \"appointment in lieu of election due to insufficiency of candidates.\" He was the only candidate, so no vote was taken and he was appointed to the seat.","source":"editorial-2026"}],"footnotesOn":["#25151 Final lists of cancelled elections: November 2020, 2022 and 2024"],"editorNotes":[{"col1":null,"col2":null,"col3":null,"heading":null,"note":null,"position":null}],"recordProvenance":"fix_gibbs_current_term.php, 2 October 2026","recordDates":[{"col1":null,"col2":null,"col3":null,"col4":null,"col5":null,"printed":null,"iso":null,"granularity":null,"label":null,"confirmed":null,"col6":null,"rejected":null}]}
{"id":23403,"section":"officeHoldings","title":"TimBen Boydston — City Council Member, The City of Santa Clarita","status":"live","holdingPerson":["#21946 TimBen Boydston"],"holdingOffice":["#18327 City Council Member"],"holdingBody":["#394 The City of Santa Clarita"],"termStart":"2006","termStartEdtf":"2006","termEnd":"April 2008","termEndEdtf":"2008-04","selectionMethod":"appointed","howEnded":"expired","startEvidence":"roster","endEvidence":"roster","footnotes":[{"col1":"1","col2":"Appointed. The roster gives TimBen Boydston \"2006-08, 2012-16\"; he won no election in 2006, and the only council vacancy of those years is the seat Cameron Smyth left in 2006 for the State Assembly. The seat was next filled at the election of April 8, 2008, at which he did not stand. Leon Worden, \"Santa Clarita City Council 1987—\", the council ledger on SCVHistory.com, carried on the page for LW3149 (archive record #4967).","col3":"editorial-2026","number":"1","note":"Appointed. The roster gives TimBen Boydston \"2006-08, 2012-16\"; he won no election in 2006, and the only council vacancy of those years is the seat Cameron Smyth left in 2006 for the State Assembly. The seat was next filled at the election of April 8, 2008, at which he did not stand. Leon Worden, \"Santa Clarita City Council 1987—\", the council ledger on SCVHistory.com, carried on the page for LW3149 (archive record #4967).","source":"editorial-2026"}],"editorNotes":[{"col1":null,"col2":null,"col3":null,"heading":null,"note":null,"position":null}],"recordProvenance":"council_winners_and_terms.php, 29 September 2026","recordDates":[{"col1":null,"col2":null,"col3":null,"col4":null,"col5":null,"printed":null,"iso":null,"granularity":null,"label":null,"confirmed":null,"col6":null,"rejected":null}]}
{"id":23401,"section":"officeHoldings","title":"Patsy Ayala — City Council Member, The City of Santa Clarita","status":"live","holdingPerson":["#23093 Patsy Ayala"],"holdingOffice":["#18327 City Council Member"],"holdingBody":["#394 The City of Santa Clarita"],"holdingDistrict":["#25153 Santa Clarita City Council, District 1"],"termStart":"December 2024","termStartEdtf":"2024-12","seatLabel":"District 1","selectionMethod":"elected","howEnded":"serving","startEvidence":"roster","footnotes":[{"col1":"1","col2":"Elected on November 5, 2024, first of 3 candidates for 1 seat, with 4,563 votes.","col3":"editorial-2026","number":"1","note":"Elected on November 5, 2024, first of 3 candidates for 1 seat, with 4,563 votes.","source":"editorial-2026"},{"col1":"2","col2":"No declaring document is held: the outcome rests on the count and on CEDA, the state's compilation of local results, which marks the same winner. California Elections Data Archive (CEDA), Center for California Studies and Institute for Social Research, California State University, Sacramento, with the Secretary of State: the 2024 candidates file (CEDA2024Data.xlsx), a compilation of the counties' returns, not a certified return.","col3":"editorial-2026","number":"2","note":"No declaring document is held: the outcome rests on the count and on CEDA, the state's compilation of local results, which marks the same winner. California Elections Data Archive (CEDA), Center for California Studies and Institute for Social Research, California State University, Sacramento, with the Secretary of State: the 2024 candidates file (CEDA2024Data.xlsx), a compilation of the counties' returns, not a certified return.","source":"editorial-2026"}],"editorNotes":[{"col1":null,"col2":null,"col3":null,"heading":null,"note":null,"position":null}],"recordProvenance":"council_winners_and_terms.php, 29 September 2026","recordDates":[{"col1":null,"col2":null,"col3":null,"col4":null,"col5":null,"printed":null,"iso":null,"granularity":null,"label":null,"confirmed":null,"col6":null,"rejected":null}]}
